<p>Israel intensified air strikes on Beirut’s southern suburbs in early March and issued large-scale evacuation warnings as fighting with the Iran-backed armed group Hezbollah escalated. Residents in areas such as Dahieh fled after the warnings and strikes; reports described packed roads as people tried to get out. The UN says the violence is fueling a fast-growing displacement crisis, with many struggling to find stable, safe shelter as conditions remain volatile. On the ground, schools and other community buildings in and around Beirut have been turned into makeshift shelters.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/2ZmPxbUnCMhF-bLD8s-OXP27DM1ZYyisJLry1pB0f4L0xquqzNb9auJ12pQldFn7TF4bt8Ag-NNR-UpkRWsh-7k30M1qkcOwLrhyQk2L611cxq-p5GCZDney_TyegjKPZ1eivPjr5T5H6_YZcFKa4ZPuE2oVo8HX0Gk01C4UvLWxkrgkIBRhrLxG3vcPz3WyJ6DDh5qmmFETIX0ZvH84C9h6gyQ6n-bHedYxJh1ufcQ0DzqgAkJkdSoj3gA1uyNAN92J73ebl6DMff4jb6w-beAbnAR6mMAfttRBox8NvYobSaQomq8UqSIVAH8-w6jqigcrOFMjf7zs3qbqr-zoq_AkdqklnWDSJ4zTTqk5CEzNVTs_jC1VZGWAzvgVB43i5ciqzWyDEhHlrYddIlKwacEh7l67kaTuC9jfMKExm51rhOQ7ugbjBqOXM_PoZWrvgVHeRJPwxknXwRNhM_LvV13DWnGZO5mxR4pC' alt='Smoke rises over Beirut after Israeli strikes as displacement grows.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Strike intensity: One account described 26 waves of attacks on Beirut as Israel widened its campaign in Lebanon.</li><li>Evacuation scope: El País said Israeli evacuation demands reached Beirut suburbs home to more than half a million people, pushing the number affected by such measures to more than 800,000.</li><li>Neighborhood spread: Le Monde described mass displacement from predominantly Shiite and Christian neighborhoods in the city’s southern areas.</li><li>Wider warning areas: The Globe and Mail said Israel issued large-scale evacuation orders for southern Lebanon and parts of Beirut amid hostilities that escalated after the U.S.-Israeli air campaign against Iran began on February 28.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UN refugee agency (UNHCR): UNHCR called the situation a “major humanitarian emergency” and said tens of thousands of Syrian refugees in Lebanon had fled back across the border. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-in-beirut-displaced-people-grapple-with-the-latest-wave-of-violence/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Displaced residents in Dahieh area: Evacuees said they left after Israeli warnings and air strikes. Some said they could not find shelter and ended up sleeping in tents, cars, or on the streets. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/videos/cg4g0gl23z4o'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Shelter residents sympathetic to Hezbollah: Some displaced people staying in an educational-center shelter criticized Israel’s actions, while also questioning the timing of Hezbollah’s rocket fire that preceded Israel’s offensive—signs of unease within parts of Hezbollah’s support base. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-06/lebanon-plunged-into-chaos-after-israels-response-to-hezbollah-war-was-inevitable-but-this-was-not-the-time.html'>El País</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-06/lebanon-plunged-into-chaos-after-israels-response-to-hezbollah-war-was-inevitable-but-this-was-not-the-time.html'>Lebanon plunged into chaos after Israel’s response to Hezbollah: ‘War was inevitable, but this was not the time’</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-israel-bombs-beirut-as-un-warns-100000-people-are-displaced/'>Israel bombs Beirut as UN warns 100,000 people are displaced</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/videos/cg4g0gl23z4o'>Beirut evacuees &#x27;sleeping in tents and cars&#x27;</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/06/world/middleeast/beirut-displaced-israeli-strikes-dahiya.html'>Families Forced to Sleep on the Streets of Beirut as Israel Pounds Hezbollah</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/03/06/lebanon-isr